<title>JAPAN: Japan bank shares fall after Tokai news.</title>
<headline>Japan bank shares fall after Tokai news.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of banks lost ground on Monday morning on expectations that banks which had financed construction firms may be hurt after general contractor Tokai Kogyo Co Ltd applied for court protection from its creditors on Friday, traders said.</p>
<p>At 0102 GMT, shares Dai-Ichi Kangyo Bank Ltd was down 40 yen at 1,460, Fuji Bank Ltd was down 50 yen at 1,560, and Sumitomo Bank Ltd was down 40 yen at 1,780.</p>
</text>
